    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d583">

                <pb facs="0686" n="590" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg590"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dudley to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima, Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-05-24"><hi rendition="#italic">May 24,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 260.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith two
                    copies and a translation of a supreme decree of the 9th instant, the purpose of
                    which is to prescribe a mode of legal proof to be followed by those desiring to
                    marry outside the Roman Catholic Church, by availing themselves of the
                    provisions of the civil marriage law of the 23d of December, 1897. The law
                    legalizes civil marriage when both parties to the contract are non-Catholics,
                    and when, one only of the parties being of that church, the ecclesiastical
                    authority refuses to perform the ceremony.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Irving B. Dudley.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d583-a1.xml" xpointer="d583-a1"/>
            </div>
